#Post: tonemapping
option.TONEMAP_MODE = Tone Mapper
option.TONEMAP_MODE.comment = The final color "film look". Each mode compresses the scene's brightness differently and has its own character: AgX is natural and keeps highlights from going neon, OKLAB is a smooth modern curve, ACES is the classic film-industry look with strong contrast, Reinhard-Gamut and Reinhard-AgX are softer custom curves with extra color protection, and GT7 imitates the vivid look of Gran Turismo 7. Purely a matter of taste - try a few.
value.TONEMAP_MODE.0 = AgX
value.TONEMAP_MODE.1 = OKLAB
value.TONEMAP_MODE.2 = ACES
value.TONEMAP_MODE.3 = Reinhard-Gamut
value.TONEMAP_MODE.4 = GT7
value.TONEMAP_MODE.5 = Reinhard-AgX
option.TONEMAP_EXPOSURE = Manual Exposure
option.TONEMAP_EXPOSURE.comment = A fixed brightness offset applied before auto exposure, measured in stops: +1.0 makes everything twice as bright, -1.0 half as bright. Use it if you consistently find the game too dark or too bright.
option.TONEMAP_SATURATION = Saturation
option.TONEMAP_SATURATION.comment = Color intensity before tone mapping: 0 removes all color (black and white), 1.0 is neutral, higher values make colors more vivid.
option.TONEMAP_STRENGTH = Tonemap Strength
option.TONEMAP_STRENGTH.comment = How much of the tone mapping is applied: 1.0 = the full film look, 0 = none at all (bright areas then clip hard to pure white and lose all detail). Lower values look flatter and harsher in highlights.
option.PURKINJE_EFFECT = Purkinje Effect
option.PURKINJE_EFFECT.comment = Simulates real human night vision: in darkness your color-sensing cells stop working and everything fades into a bluish grey. Dark scenes lose their color the same way, so nights feel darker and more atmospheric without actually removing any light. Needs Auto Exposure (AE) so the game knows how dark it is.
option.PURKINJE_STRENGTH = Purkinje Strength
option.PURKINJE_STRENGTH.comment = How strong the night-time bluish-grey shift is: 0 = off, 1 = full effect in the darkest scenes.
option.TONEMAP_AGX_LOOK = AgX Look
option.TONEMAP_AGX_LOOK.comment = A preset style applied inside the AgX tone mapper (only active in AgX mode): Base is neutral, Punchy adds contrast and saturation, Greyscale is black and white.
value.TONEMAP_AGX_LOOK.0 = Base
value.TONEMAP_AGX_LOOK.1 = Punchy
value.TONEMAP_AGX_LOOK.2 = Greyscale
option.TONEMAP_AGX_CONTRAST = AgX Contrast
option.TONEMAP_AGX_CONTRAST.comment = Midtone contrast in AgX mode: higher makes darks darker and lights brighter around the middle of the image; lower looks flatter and softer.
option.TONEMAP_AGX_SATURATION = AgX Saturation
option.TONEMAP_AGX_SATURATION.comment = Color intensity after AgX tone mapping: 1.0 is neutral, higher = more vivid colors, lower = washed out.
option.TONEMAP_AGX_GAMMA = AgX Gamma
option.TONEMAP_AGX_GAMMA.comment = Overall midtone brightness in AgX mode: values below 1.0 brighten the image, values above 1.0 darken it.
option.TONEMAP_OKLAB_OVEREXPOSURE = Oklab DRT Overexposure
option.TONEMAP_OKLAB_OVEREXPOSURE.comment = Controls how bright highlights can get in OKLAB mode before they flatten into white. Higher values let bright areas keep climbing and hold detail longer. Normal midtone brightness is unaffected at any value.
option.TONEMAP_RG_GAMUT_EXPANSION = Reinhard-Gamut Expansion
option.TONEMAP_RG_GAMUT_EXPANSION.comment = Bright-color protection in Reinhard-Gamut mode: very saturated highlights are gently pulled toward neutral before the tone curve so they don't turn neon or shift color. 0 = off, higher = stronger protection.
option.TONEMAP_RG_INPUT_SCALE = Reinhard-Gamut Input Scale
option.TONEMAP_RG_INPUT_SCALE.comment = Overall image brightness in Reinhard-Gamut mode before the tone curve. The default value keeps middle grey exactly correct; higher = brighter image, lower = darker.
option.TONEMAP_RG_HIGHLIGHT_REACH_EV = Reinhard-Gamut Highlight Reach
option.TONEMAP_RG_HIGHLIGHT_REACH_EV.comment = How many brightness doublings above middle grey a light source needs before it hits pure white in Reinhard-Gamut mode. Higher = highlights compress more gently and keep detail longer; lower = bright things turn white sooner.
option.TONEMAP_RG_HUE_RETENTION = Reinhard-Gamut Hue Retention
option.TONEMAP_RG_HUE_RETENTION.comment = How strongly very bright colors keep their original color instead of drifting (for example a red glare staying red instead of turning orange-white). 0 = allow drift, 1 = hold the original color as much as possible.
option.TONEMAP_RA_GAMUT_EXPANSION = Reinhard-AgX Expansion
option.TONEMAP_RA_GAMUT_EXPANSION.comment = The same bright-color protection as Reinhard-Gamut, for Reinhard-AgX mode: pulls very saturated highlights toward neutral before compression. 0 = off, higher = stronger.
option.TONEMAP_RA_INPUT_SCALE = Reinhard-AgX Input Scale
option.TONEMAP_RA_INPUT_SCALE.comment = Overall image brightness in Reinhard-AgX mode before the tone curve. The default keeps middle grey correct; higher = brighter, lower = darker.
option.TONEMAP_RA_COMPRESSION_START = Reinhard-AgX Compression Start
option.TONEMAP_RA_COMPRESSION_START.comment = The brightness level where Reinhard-AgX stops displaying the image as-is and starts compressing highlights. Higher = more of the image stays untouched; lower = compression already begins in the darker tones.
option.TONEMAP_RA_HIGHLIGHT_REACH_EV = Reinhard-AgX Highlight Reach
option.TONEMAP_RA_HIGHLIGHT_REACH_EV.comment = How bright something must be (in brightness doublings above middle grey) before it reaches pure white in Reinhard-AgX mode. Higher = gentler, more detailed highlights.
option.TONEMAP_RA_SHOULDER_POWER = Reinhard-AgX Shoulder Power
option.TONEMAP_RA_SHOULDER_POWER.comment = The shape of the highlight compression in Reinhard-AgX mode: higher values keep normal brightness exact for longer and then compress very bright areas faster.
option.TONEMAP_RA_HUE_RETENTION = Reinhard-AgX Hue Retention
option.TONEMAP_RA_HUE_RETENTION.comment = How strongly very bright colors keep their original color instead of drifting toward white or another hue. 0 = allow drift, 1 = maximum color fidelity.
option.TONEMAP_GT7_BLEND = GT7 Path Blend
option.TONEMAP_GT7_BLEND.comment = Mixes the two halves of the GT7-style tone mapper: 0 = only the contrasty per-channel curve, 1 = only the path where bright colors wash out toward white like film highlights. The official default is 0.6.
option.TONEMAP_GT7_CHROMA_FADE_START = GT7 Chroma Fade Start
option.TONEMAP_GT7_CHROMA_FADE_START.comment = The brightness level (relative to paper white) where colors start washing out toward white, like a camera overexposing a bright light source. Lower = the washing starts earlier.
option.TONEMAP_GT7_CHROMA_FADE_END = GT7 Chroma Fade End
option.TONEMAP_GT7_CHROMA_FADE_END.comment = The brightness level where colors are fully washed out to white. Keep it above the fade start; the official default is 1.16.

#Post: camera & effects
option.DOF = Depth of Field
option.DOF.comment = Blurs whatever your crosshair is not focused on, like a real camera lens: near and far objects soften while the aimed-at spot stays sharp. Costs performance.
option.MOTION_BLUR = Motion Blur
option.MOTION_BLUR.comment = Smears the image slightly while you turn or move quickly, like a real camera sensor. Reduces strobing, but adds motion trails.
option.MB_STRENGTH = Motion Blur Strength
option.MB_STRENGTH.comment = Length of the motion smear: 0 = barely visible, 1 = strong trails.
option.BLOOM = Bloom
option.BLOOM.comment = Makes very bright things glow and bleed light into their surroundings - the haze around a torch flame, or glare when you look toward the sun.
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH = Bloom Strength
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH.comment = Strength of the glow.
option.AE = Auto Exposure
option.AE.comment = Automatic eye adaptation, like a phone camera's auto brightness: walk into a cave and the image gradually brightens; step into sunlight and it dims. Off = one fixed manual brightness.
option.AE_TARGET_LUMINANCE = Auto Exposure Target
option.AE_TARGET_LUMINANCE.comment = The average brightness auto exposure aims for: lower = the whole game renders darker and moodier, higher = brighter. 0.18 is the standard neutral value.
option.AE_ADAPTATION_STRENGTH = Auto Exposure Adaptation
option.AE_ADAPTATION_STRENGTH.comment = How strongly the exposure follows the scene. 0 = never react (fixed brightness everywhere); 1 = nearly every scene gets equalized to the same average brightness, which flattens natural contrast. In between keeps some of the game's own light differences.

#Post: antialiasing
option.TAA = TAA
option.TAA.comment = Removes jagged staircase edges by blending many frames together. Very effective, but costs performance and can leave faint trails behind fast-moving objects.
option.CAS = CAS Sharpening
option.CAS.comment = A light sharpening filter (AMD FidelityFX CAS) applied on top, mainly to restore the crispness that antialiasing smoothing softens away.
option.CAS_SHARPNESS = CAS Sharpness
option.CAS_SHARPNESS.comment = Sharpening strength: 0 = off, higher = crisper (too high shows bright halos around edges).

#Post: color dither
option.COLOR_DITHER_STRENGTH = Color Dither Strength
option.COLOR_DITHER_STRENGTH.comment = Adds an almost invisible fine grain that hides color banding - the ugly striped rings you can otherwise see in smooth sky, fog and shadow gradients. The default 1.0 is a good balance; higher = stronger de-banding but slightly more visible grain.

#Clouds: temporal upscaling values
value.CLOUD_TEMPORAL_UPSCALING.1 = 1x (Full)
value.CLOUD_TEMPORAL_UPSCALING.2 = 2x
value.CLOUD_TEMPORAL_UPSCALING.3 = 3x
value.CLOUD_TEMPORAL_UPSCALING.4 = 4x

#Clouds: rendering
option.VOLUMETRIC_CLOUDS = Volumetric Clouds
option.VOLUMETRIC_CLOUDS.comment = Replaces flat cloud pictures with real 3D clouds that have volume, depth and proper sunlight. One of the most expensive effects in the pack.
option.CIRRUS = Cirrus Clouds
option.CIRRUS.comment = Thin high-altitude cloud shell with silver-lining lighting. Far cheaper than the volumetric layer and independent of it: turning Volumetric Clouds off keeps the cirrus, and vice versa.
option.CLOUD_TEMPORAL_UPSCALING = Temporal Upscaling
option.CLOUD_TEMPORAL_UPSCALING.comment = Renders clouds at a reduced resolution and rebuilds full detail over consecutive frames. 1x = full resolution (sharpest, slowest), 4x = quarter resolution (fastest, can smear slightly during fast camera movement).
option.CLOUD_AGE_LIMIT = Cloud History Age Limit
option.CLOUD_AGE_LIMIT.comment = How many frames a cloud texel's accumulated history stays trusted before a fresh sample fully replaces it: higher = steadier clouds between frames, but slower response to wind and view changes.
option.CLOUD_VIEW_MIN_STEPS = Min March Steps
option.CLOUD_VIEW_MIN_STEPS.comment = Sampling quality for clouds near you: higher = fewer holes or speckles on nearby cloud edges, slower.
option.CLOUD_VIEW_MAX_STEPS = Max March Steps
option.CLOUD_VIEW_MAX_STEPS.comment = Sampling quality for clouds far toward the horizon: higher = clouds stay detailed farther away, slower.
option.CLOUD_VIEW_TARGET_STEP_KM = Target Step Distance
option.CLOUD_VIEW_TARGET_STEP_KM.comment = How densely clouds are scanned along your line of sight (smaller = finer steps). Lower = more detail and smoother shapes, slower.
option.CLOUD_LIGHT_STEPS = Light Steps
option.CLOUD_LIGHT_STEPS.comment = How carefully sunlight is traced through each cloud to decide which parts are in shadow. Higher = better lit and shadowed detail inside clouds, slower.
option.CLOUD_BASE_ALTITUDE = Base Altitude
option.CLOUD_BASE_ALTITUDE.comment = How high above the terrain the cloud layer floats. Higher = clouds sit farther overhead.
suffix.CLOUD_BASE_ALTITUDE = km
option.CLOUD_THICKNESS_KM = Layer Thickness
option.CLOUD_THICKNESS_KM.comment = Vertical thickness of the cloud layer: higher = taller, towering clouds with deeper shadows inside.
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE = Coverage
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE.comment = How much of the sky is covered: higher = wide, connected cloud decks; lower = scattered clouds and more blue sky.
option.CLOUD_DISTRIBUTION_SCALE_KM = Distribution Scale
option.CLOUD_DISTRIBUTION_SCALE_KM.comment = The size of the overall cloud pattern across the world: higher = bigger, more sprawling cloud systems spaced farther apart; lower = more, smaller cloud clusters.
option.CLOUD_WIND_SPEED = Wind Speed
option.CLOUD_WIND_SPEED.comment = How fast clouds drift across the sky.
option.CLOUD_FINE_WIND_FACTOR = Fine Wind Factor
option.CLOUD_FINE_WIND_FACTOR.comment = Makes the small details inside a cloud flow faster than the cloud as a whole, so clouds seem to boil and churn instead of just sliding by.
option.CLOUD_EROSION_SCALE_KM = Erosion Scale
option.CLOUD_EROSION_SCALE_KM.comment = The size of the big billows that break up the cloud outlines: higher = broad, smooth shapes; lower = more broken-up, wispy clouds.
option.CLOUD_EROSION_STRENGTH = Erosion Strength
option.CLOUD_EROSION_STRENGTH.comment = How strongly those billows eat into the cloud: higher = more ragged, torn shapes; lower = rounder, denser blobs.
option.CLOUD_FINE_EROSION_SCALE_KM = Fine Erosion Scale
option.CLOUD_FINE_EROSION_SCALE_KM.comment = The size of the small wispy details on top of the big shapes: lower = finer, sharper little tendrils.
option.CLOUD_FINE_EROSION_STRENGTH = Fine Erosion Strength
option.CLOUD_FINE_EROSION_STRENGTH.comment = Strength of the small wispy details: higher = more fine detail and ragged edges.
option.CLOUD_FINE_EROSION_HEIGHT = Fine Erosion Height
option.CLOUD_FINE_EROSION_HEIGHT.comment = Where inside the cloud (bottom to top) the fine detail reaches full strength: lower = detail concentrated near the cloud base, higher = spread up toward the top.
option.CLOUD_DENSITY_MULTIPLIER = Density Multiplier
option.CLOUD_DENSITY_MULTIPLIER.comment = Overall thickness of the clouds: higher = denser, heavier clouds that block more light and cast stronger shading.
option.CLOUD_LIGHT_MAX_DISTANCE_KM = Light Trace Distance
option.CLOUD_LIGHT_MAX_DISTANCE_KM.comment = How far sunlight is traced through a cloud when deciding its self-shadowing: higher = correct lighting deeper inside thick clouds, slower.
option.CLOUD_PHASE_FORWARD_G = Forward Phase G
option.CLOUD_PHASE_FORWARD_G.comment = Controls the bright "silver lining" when you look toward the sun through clouds: higher = a tighter, brighter glow around the sun.
option.CLOUD_PHASE_BACKWARD_G = Backward Phase G
option.CLOUD_PHASE_BACKWARD_G.comment = Controls how bright clouds look when your back is to the sun: higher = a stronger glow on the clouds across the sky from the sun.
option.CLOUD_MS_ALBEDO = Cloud Albedo
option.CLOUD_MS_ALBEDO.comment = How much light a cloud particle scatters instead of absorbing. Water clouds barely absorb, so this sits close to 1: lower = greyer, heavier clouds with darker interiors.
option.CLOUD_MS_VOLUME = Volume Scatter
option.CLOUD_MS_VOLUME.comment = Strength of the isotropic light that fills the inside of a thick cloud. This is what keeps shadowed cloud interiors from going black: higher = brighter, milkier cores.
option.CLOUD_MS_VOLUME_FALLOFF = Volume Depth Falloff
option.CLOUD_MS_VOLUME_FALLOFF.comment = How fast that interior light fades as sunlight has to travel farther into the cloud: lower = light reaches deeper, so tall clouds stay lit further down.
option.CLOUD_SKY_LIGHT_STRENGTH = Sky Light Strength
option.CLOUD_SKY_LIGHT_STRENGTH.comment = How much ambient sky light the clouds receive: higher = brighter shadowed sides and undersides, so clouds look softer and whiter.
option.CLOUD_HISTORY_GUIDED_END_SCALE = History Guided Scale
option.CLOUD_HISTORY_GUIDED_END_SCALE.comment = Safety margin for an experimental speed-up that stops scanning clouds early using the previous frame's data; only used when that feature is active. Higher = stops later (safer image, smaller saving).

#Shadows
option.SHADOW_PCSS = PCSS Shadows
option.SHADOW_PCSS.comment = Realistic soft shadows: a shadow's edge gets blurrier the farther the object is above the ground it falls on, like real sunlight. Off (Low) = cheap hard-edged shadows. The thickness estimate needed for light-through-leaves keeps working either way.
option.shadowMapResolution = Shadow Map Resolution
option.shadowMapResolution.comment = Detail level of the shadow map: higher = sharper, cleaner shadow edges that also stay crisp farther from you, at a significant performance cost.
option.SHADOW_BLOCKER_SAMPLES = PCSS Blocker Samples
option.SHADOW_BLOCKER_SAMPLES.comment = Precision of the soft-shadow measurement (how exactly the game estimates how high above the ground a shadow caster sits): higher = smoother, more stable soft edges, slower.
option.SHADOW_BLOCKER_SEARCH_TEXELS = PCSS Search Radius
option.SHADOW_BLOCKER_SEARCH_TEXELS.comment = How wide an area is examined for that measurement: higher = allows broader, softer shadows, slower.
option.SHADOW_SUN_ANGULAR_RADIUS = Sun Angular Radius
option.SHADOW_SUN_ANGULAR_RADIUS.comment = The apparent size of the sun in the sky. A bigger sun gives softer shadows overall, like a hazy day; smaller = crisper shadows.
option.SHADOW_BLOCKER_DEPTH_TOLERANCE_METERS = Blocker Depth Tolerance
option.SHADOW_BLOCKER_DEPTH_TOLERANCE_METERS.comment = Lets surfaces at nearly the same height count as the ground. A small value can reduce shadow speckle on stairs, fences and leaves; too high makes shadows leak through thin objects. 0 = strictest.
option.SHADOW_PCF_MIN_SAMPLES = PCF Min Samples
option.SHADOW_PCF_MIN_SAMPLES.comment = Smoothness of shadow edges in fully sunlit areas: higher = less grainy edges, slower.
option.SHADOW_PCF_MAX_SAMPLES = PCF Max Samples
option.SHADOW_PCF_MAX_SAMPLES.comment = Smoothness in the softest, blurriest shadow regions: higher = cleaner large soft shadows, slower.
option.SHADOW_PCF_GAIN = PCF Sample Gain
option.SHADOW_PCF_GAIN.comment = How aggressively the filter spends more samples as shadows get softer: higher = better quality in soft regions at higher cost.
option.SHADOW_SUN_HEIGHT_BOOST = Sun Height Boost
option.SHADOW_SUN_HEIGHT_BOOST.comment = Extra softening at sunrise and sunset, when real shadows are naturally long and diffuse.
option.SHADOW_DISTANCE_BOOST = Distance Boost
option.SHADOW_DISTANCE_BOOST.comment = Makes shadows progressively blurrier with distance from you, like real life; this also hides the shadow map's range limit.
option.SHADOW_CONTACT_SHARPEN_TEXELS = Contact Sharpen
option.SHADOW_CONTACT_SHARPEN_TEXELS.comment = Keeps the line where an object touches the ground crisp, so soft shadows don't smear the contact point.
option.SHADOW_SSS = Plant SSS
option.SHADOW_SSS.comment = Lets dense foliage glow when backlit, using a shadow-map thickness estimate. Off removes the effect and its extra shadow-map sampling; the SSS sliders only apply while it is on.
option.SHADOW_SSS_STEPS = SSS Steps
option.SHADOW_SSS_STEPS.comment = Quality of the light-through-leaves effect (how precisely the light path inside foliage is traced): higher = smoother glow, slower.
option.SHADOW_SSS_DENSITY = SSS Density
option.SHADOW_SSS_DENSITY.comment = How strongly leaves absorb light: higher = less light passes through thick foliage; lower = leaves glow more.
option.SHADOW_SSS_SCALE = SSS Scale
option.SHADOW_SSS_SCALE.comment = Size of the foliage the effect assumes: higher = light travels farther inside leaves before exiting, giving a broader glow.
option.SHADOW_SSS_PENUMBRA_BOOST = SSS Penumbra Boost
option.SHADOW_SSS_PENUMBRA_BOOST.comment = Widens the soft edges of the through-leaf glow.
option.SHADOW_SSS_ENERGY = SSS Energy Share
option.SHADOW_SSS_ENERGY.comment = The maximum share of direct sunlight that can be turned into through-leaf glow: higher = foliage lit from behind glows more strongly.
option.SHADOW_SSS_DEBUG = SSS Debug View
option.SHADOW_SSS_DEBUG.comment = Troubleshooting view that shows only the through-leaf light. Leave Off while playing.
value.SHADOW_SSS_DEBUG.0 = Off
value.SHADOW_SSS_DEBUG.1 = On
option.SHADOW_SSS_PHASE_G = SSS Phase G
option.SHADOW_SSS_PHASE_G.comment = Direction of the through-leaf glow: higher = brightest when you look toward the sun through the plant, like real backlit leaves.
option.SHADOW_SSS_FADE_START = SSS Fade Start
option.SHADOW_SSS_FADE_START.comment = The through-leaf glow fades out near the edge of the shadow map's coverage; this sets how close to the edge the fading begins (higher = the effect survives farther out).
option.CONTACT_SHADOWS = Contact Shadows
option.CONTACT_SHADOWS.comment = Small-scale shadows computed directly from the 3D scene. They fill in detail the shadow map misses - objects right at your feet - and keep working beyond the shadow map's range.
value.CONTACT_SHADOWS.0 = Off
value.CONTACT_SHADOWS.1 = On
option.CONTACT_SHADOW_STEPS = Contact Shadow Steps
option.CONTACT_SHADOW_STEPS.comment = Quality of these small shadows: higher = fewer missed or speckled shadows, slower.
option.CONTACT_SHADOW_MAX_DISTANCE = Contact Shadow Distance
option.CONTACT_SHADOW_MAX_DISTANCE.comment = Maximum reach of the effect in metres; the actual reach also scales with your view distance.
suffix.CONTACT_SHADOW_MAX_DISTANCE = m
option.CONTACT_SHADOW_THICKNESS = Contact Shadow Thickness
option.CONTACT_SHADOW_THICKNESS.comment = Assumed thickness of the objects casting these shadows: higher = more forgiving and softer; lower = sharper but can miss thin blockers.
option.CONTACT_SHADOW_DEBUG = Contact Shadow Debug
option.CONTACT_SHADOW_DEBUG.comment = Diagnostic views for troubleshooting: the raw shadow mask, or an exaggerated darkness view. Leave Off while playing.
value.CONTACT_SHADOW_DEBUG.0 = Off
value.CONTACT_SHADOW_DEBUG.1 = Raw Mask
value.CONTACT_SHADOW_DEBUG.2 = Boosted

#AO
option.AO_MODE = Ambient Occlusion Mode
option.AO_MODE.comment = Ambient occlusion: the soft darkening inside corners, crevices and where objects meet the ground that makes the world look grounded. GTAO is the efficient standard method; SSAO is an alternative with a slightly different look that costs more. Off = flat lighting without corner darkening.
value.AO_MODE.0 = Off
value.AO_MODE.1 = GTAO
value.AO_MODE.2 = SSAO
option.AO_TEMPORAL = Temporal Accumulation
option.AO_TEMPORAL.comment = Smooths the corner darkening across several frames so it looks clean instead of grainy. Off = noisier but reacts instantly, with no smoothing lag.
option.GTAO_SLICES = GTAO Slices
option.GTAO_SLICES.comment = Quality of the corner-darkening calculation: higher = smoother and more accurate, slower.
option.GTAO_HORIZON_STEPS = GTAO Horizon Steps
option.GTAO_HORIZON_STEPS.comment = How far the calculation looks along each direction: higher = catches larger nearby objects, slower.
option.GTAO_RADIUS = GTAO Radius
option.GTAO_RADIUS.comment = How far away an object can darken its surroundings, in metres: higher = broader, softer corner shadows.
suffix.GTAO_RADIUS = m
option.GTAO_STRENGTH = GTAO Strength
option.GTAO_STRENGTH.comment = How dark the corners get.
option.GTAO_MULTIBOUNCE = GTAO Multi-Bounce
option.GTAO_MULTIBOUNCE.comment = Lets bright surfaces bounce a little light back into the corners, so dark corners take on a slight tint of their surroundings instead of going pure black.
option.GTAO_FALLOFF_START = GTAO Falloff Start
option.GTAO_FALLOFF_START.comment = Where inside the radius the darkening starts to fade out: lower = tight dark contact lines, higher = the darkening spreads more evenly.
option.AO_AGE_LIMIT = AO History Age Limit
option.AO_AGE_LIMIT.comment = How many frames of smoothing are blended before a result counts as settled: higher = smoother, but corner darkening reacts more slowly to changes.
option.AO_HISTORY_DISTANCE_LIMIT = AO History Distance Limit
option.AO_HISTORY_DISTANCE_LIMIT.comment = How far something may move between frames before its stored smoothing is thrown away: lower = fewer smears when things move, possibly more grain.
option.AO_HISTORY_NORMAL_DOT_MIN = AO History Normal Limit
option.AO_HISTORY_NORMAL_DOT_MIN.comment = How strictly a surface must keep facing the same direction for its stored smoothing to be reused: higher = fewer smears when turning the camera, possibly more grain.
option.SSAO_SAMPLES = SSAO Samples
option.SSAO_SAMPLES.comment = Quality of the alternative SSAO mode: higher = smoother corner darkening, slower.
option.SSAO_RADIUS = SSAO Radius
option.SSAO_RADIUS.comment = How far away an object can darken its surroundings, in metres.
suffix.SSAO_RADIUS = m
option.SSAO_STRENGTH = SSAO Strength
option.SSAO_STRENGTH.comment = How dark the corners get. SSAO reads lighter than GTAO, so its default is intentionally steeper.
option.AO_DARKEN_SLOWDOWN = AO Darken Slowdown
option.AO_DARKEN_SLOWDOWN.comment = Slows the fade-in of new darkening so added shadows appear like a natural light change instead of a sudden noisy pop. Lower = gentler; 1.0 = no slowing.

#Water
option.WATER_SSR = Water SSR
option.WATER_SSR.comment = Lets water reflect the actual world in front of it - mountains, buildings, trees - instead of only the sky.
option.WATER_SSR_STEPS = Water SSR Quality
option.WATER_SSR_STEPS.comment = Reflection quality: higher = reflections reach farther with fewer broken or faded areas, slower.
option.WATER_POM = Water Parallax
option.WATER_POM.comment = Gives the wave surface real 3D depth: waves visibly rise and shift as you move past. Off = flat water with painted-on wave shading.
option.OCEAN_POM_COARSE_STEPS = POM Coarse Steps
option.OCEAN_POM_COARSE_STEPS.comment = Quality of the wave-depth search: higher = more accurate wave relief, slower.
option.OCEAN_POM_BISECT_STEPS = POM Bisection Steps
option.OCEAN_POM_BISECT_STEPS.comment = Refinement passes that sharpen the wave relief after the coarse search: higher = crisper wave crests, slower.
option.WATER_FOG_CAUSTICS = Water Caustics
option.WATER_FOG_CAUSTICS.comment = Underwater, waves focus and scatter sunlight, producing moving bright patterns in the water haze - like real caustic light patterns on a pool floor.
option.WATER_FOG_CAUSTIC_STRENGTH = Caustic Strength
option.WATER_FOG_CAUSTIC_STRENGTH.comment = Intensity of those underwater light patterns.
option.EPIPOLAR_VOLUMETRICS = Epipolar Volumetric Light
option.EPIPOLAR_VOLUMETRICS.comment = Draws epipolar sunlight shafts through participating media (underwater god rays and air light shafts), correctly shadowed by terrain.
option.EPIPOLAR_SLICES = Epipolar Slices
option.EPIPOLAR_SLICES.comment = Resolution of the light-shaft grid across the screen: higher = crisper, more stable rays, slower.
value.EPIPOLAR_SLICES.256 = 256
value.EPIPOLAR_SLICES.512 = 512
value.EPIPOLAR_SLICES.1024 = 1024
value.EPIPOLAR_SLICES.2048 = 2048
option.EPIPOLAR_SAMPLES = Epipolar Samples
option.EPIPOLAR_SAMPLES.comment = Detail along each light ray: higher = smoother shafts, slower.
value.EPIPOLAR_SAMPLES.128 = 128
value.EPIPOLAR_SAMPLES.256 = 256
value.EPIPOLAR_SAMPLES.512 = 512
value.EPIPOLAR_SAMPLES.1024 = 1024
option.EPIPOLAR_SHADOW_STEPS = Epipolar Shadow Steps
option.EPIPOLAR_SHADOW_STEPS.comment = How carefully each point of a ray checks whether sunlight is blocked: higher = shadow detail inside the water, slower.
option.WATER_EPIPOLAR_MAX_DISTANCE = Water Epipolar March Distance
option.WATER_EPIPOLAR_MAX_DISTANCE.comment = How far underwater the shadow calculation runs precisely; beyond this distance the water is simply treated as sunlit. Lower = less noise, but far water loses shadow detail.
suffix.WATER_EPIPOLAR_MAX_DISTANCE = m
option.EPIPOLAR_DEPTH_TOLERANCE = Epipolar Depth Tolerance
option.EPIPOLAR_DEPTH_TOLERANCE.comment = How leniently neighbouring pixels may share each other's results: higher = fewer artifacts but slightly blurrier rays.
option.EPIPOLAR_EDGE_SHARPEN = Epipolar Edge Sharpen
option.EPIPOLAR_EDGE_SHARPEN.comment = Sharpens the edges of the light shafts against their surroundings.
option.EPIPOLAR_EDGE_EXTEND = Epipolar Edge Extend
option.EPIPOLAR_EDGE_EXTEND.comment = How far the effect searches for a valid neighbouring sample when a pixel has none: higher = fewer holes or gaps in the rays.

#Fog
option.AIR_FOG = Air Fog
option.AIR_FOG.comment = Distance haze: faraway terrain gently fades toward the horizon, like real atmospheric perspective.
option.AIR_FOG_INTENSITY = Fog Intensity
option.AIR_FOG_INTENSITY.comment = Overall strength of the haze.
option.AIR_FOG_DENSITY = Fog Density
option.AIR_FOG_DENSITY.comment = Base thickness of the haze: higher = terrain disappears at shorter distances.
option.AIR_FOG_SKY_STRENGTH = Sky Fog Strength
option.AIR_FOG_SKY_STRENGTH.comment = How much the haze picks up the sky's color instead of staying a neutral grey.
option.AIR_FOG_SHADOWS = Fog Shadows
option.AIR_FOG_SHADOWS.comment = Lets shadows appear inside the haze: cloud shadows darken the mist and sunlit gaps glow, giving the air itself a sense of depth.
option.BOUNDARY_FOG = Boundary Fog
option.BOUNDARY_FOG.comment = Hides the edge of the rendered world by fading distant terrain into the sky, so the loaded-chunk boundary is not a hard wall.
option.BOUNDARY_FOG_START = Boundary Fog Start
option.BOUNDARY_FOG_START.comment = Where the hiding fade begins, as a fraction of your render distance: higher = the fade hugs the visible edge, lower = terrain fades earlier.
option.BOUNDARY_FOG_STRENGTH = Boundary Fog Strength
option.BOUNDARY_FOG_STRENGTH.comment = How opaque the edge-hiding haze is.
option.BOUNDARY_FOG_HEIGHT_FADE = Boundary Fog Height Fade
option.BOUNDARY_FOG_HEIGHT_FADE.comment = How much the edge haze weakens when looking up at the sky, so the horizon is masked without a milky sky overhead.

#Lighting
option.OPAQUE_REFLECTION = Opaque Reflections
option.OPAQUE_REFLECTION.comment = Lets shiny solid blocks reflect the actual scene around them. Off = only a generic sky-based sheen remains.
value.OPAQUE_REFLECTION.0 = Off
value.OPAQUE_REFLECTION.1 = On
option.OPAQUE_SSR_QUALITY = Opaque Reflection Quality
option.OPAQUE_SSR_QUALITY.comment = Quality of true scene reflections on solid blocks: Environment Only = cheap sky sheen for everything; Medium/High/Ultra raise the accuracy and reach of real reflections.
value.OPAQUE_SSR_QUALITY.0 = Environment Only
value.OPAQUE_SSR_QUALITY.1 = Medium
value.OPAQUE_SSR_QUALITY.2 = High
value.OPAQUE_SSR_QUALITY.3 = Ultra
option.OPAQUE_REFLECTION_ROUGHNESS_THRESHOLD = Opaque Reflection Roughness Threshold
option.OPAQUE_REFLECTION_ROUGHNESS_THRESHOLD.comment = How matte a surface may be before it stops mirroring the scene and falls back to the cheap sky sheen: higher = more surfaces get real reflections (more cost); lower = only near-mirror surfaces do.
option.OPAQUE_REFLECTION_ROUGHNESS_TRANSITION = Opaque Reflection Roughness Transition
option.OPAQUE_REFLECTION_ROUGHNESS_TRANSITION.comment = Width of the gradual blend between real reflections and the sky sheen, so surfaces don't visibly pop between the two.
option.GI_MODE = Global Illumination
option.GI_MODE.comment = Bounced sunlight: light that lands on a surface and then softly tints its surroundings, like red carpet glowing onto nearby walls. Off keeps direct light and ambient only. SSGI computes the bounce from what is on screen; Reflective Shadow Map computes it from the sun's shadow map for more stable results over a wider area. Both fill the gaps with normal sky light.
value.GI_MODE.0 = None
value.GI_MODE.1 = SSGI
value.GI_MODE.2 = Reflective Shadow Map
screen.SSGI = Screen Space GI
screen.RSM = Reflective Shadow Map
option.RSM_SAMPLES = RSM Samples
option.RSM_SAMPLES.comment = How many bounce-light samples each pixel gathers per frame: higher = smoother, more detailed colored bounce light, slower.
option.RSM_RADIUS = RSM Radius
option.RSM_RADIUS.comment = How wide an area each pixel gathers bounce light from, in metres: higher = broader, softer color bleeding.
suffix.RSM_RADIUS = m
option.GI_DENOISE = GI Temporal Denoising
option.GI_DENOISE.comment = Smooths the bounce light across consecutive frames to remove grain. Off shows the raw, noisy bounce light.
option.GI_HISTORY_FRAMES = GI History Length
option.GI_HISTORY_FRAMES.comment = How many frames of bounce light are blended together: higher = cleaner and steadier, but lighting changes (placing torches, the moving sun) settle slightly later.
option.SSGI_STEPS = SSGI March Steps
option.SSGI_STEPS.comment = Depth samples traced per pixel: higher = smoother, more detailed bounce light in the distance, slower.
option.SSGI_MARCH_PIXELS = SSGI March Width
option.SSGI_MARCH_PIXELS.comment = How far the bounce-light ray marches across the screen, in pixels: higher = bounce light reaches farther from its source, slower.
option.SSGI_THICKNESS = SSGI Thickness
option.SSGI_THICKNESS.comment = Assumed depth thickness of the surfaces hit by the rays, in meters: higher = thin geometry blocks bounce light more (less leak-through), lower = more light passes through thin surfaces.
suffix.SSGI_THICKNESS = m
option.SSGI_RADIANCE_LIMIT = SSGI Radiance Clamp
option.SSGI_RADIANCE_LIMIT.comment = Upper bound on the stored bounce light: lower = fewer bright firefly sparkles but dimmer highlight bounce; raise only for unusually bright scenes.
option.RSM_STRENGTH = RSM Strength
option.RSM_STRENGTH.comment = Intensity of the bounced sunlight. Does not change the direct sun or the ambient sky light.
option.RSM_SKY_OCCLUSION = RSM Sky Occlusion
option.RSM_SKY_OCCLUSION.comment = Darkens the bounce-light sky glow in areas the shadow map shows are shielded from the sky (roofs, dense foliage). Off removes the effect and skips its sampling.
option.RSM_SKY_OCCLUSION_FLOOR = RSM Minimum Sky Factor
option.RSM_SKY_OCCLUSION_FLOOR.comment = In areas the shadow data shows are shielded from the sky, this limits the leftover sky glow: lower = darker, more natural enclosed spaces; 1.0 = no extra limiting. Only applies while RSM Sky Occlusion is on.
option.RSM_DEBUG = RSM Debug
option.RSM_DEBUG.comment = Diagnostic views for troubleshooting the bounce light. Leave on Scene while playing.
